                                                                        "checked": false,
                                                                        "text": ". It costs $1,000 less than the Naturepedic and has four firmness options on each side, with a much softer Plush than the EOS Classic. I slept really well on the Bedgear M3 Performance, but it isn't made of organic materials, runs a little hot, has poor edge support, and has a short trial period (just 30 nights). It's a memory foam hybrid, and the coils influence the various firmness. Read my full ",
